Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::readiness_refuses_a_repeated_first_draw_of_at_least_eight_bytes`.

The defect: the repeat rule is off by one and judges only draws longer than `MAXIMUM_BYTES`. A
draw of exactly eight bytes, the width the instruction backend draws, then passes as `READY`
although every byte is the same.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `STEP_FIRST_ALL_SAME`, with a draw of exactly
eight equal nonzero bytes.

diff --git a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
